{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: fresh review of the corrected exact head b39bd2adb7b0eed3bb491914aee9afa21a95a4de on request/refuse-before-signing (pushed), five commits over main c3cc0e44, answering your changes-requested verdict bf03b5f1 on e76b508f (ratified). Seventeen artifacts stand at this head and are the whole diff against main, now including internal/intent/intent.go and its test. The reporting artifact is the cmd/gs/preflight.go artifact: name it first and rest on all seventeen.\n\nFinding 1: app.PreflightChain folds a labeled chain into a scratch fold of its own with each $label resolved to its prospective event id, so a malformed act behind a label refuses at its position with nothing appended, and a chain that only its own earlier acts make valid is admitted (TestPreflightJudgesALabeledChainInOrder, TestPreflightAdmitsAChainThatOnlyItsOwnEarlierActsMakeValid, TestPreflightLeavesTheProjectionUnchangedWhenItRefusesAChain). Finding 2: --kind on state, --text on supersede, --verdict on review and batch's per-act shape are settled before a repository is opened or a key is read, each tested with the key file removed. Finding 3: the raw scan is gone; parseRefusal classifies the flag parser's own refusal after values and -- are consumed (TestAValueThatLooksLikeAFlagIsNotAMistake in three spellings; TestTheGenuinePositionalMistakeIsStillHelpful). Finding 4: intent.DedupIdentityFor spells the dedup identity from the roster fingerprint, and heldUnderKey asks kernel.PriorAct with no private key, so an act already accepted under the key is left to the sequencer to replay, for a single act and for a chain (TestPreflightReplaysAnAcceptedActAfterItsWorldMoved, TestPreflightReplaysAnAcceptedChainAfterItsWorldMoved); a different act under the same key is still refused by the kernel. Your four probes are green unmodified; TestCodexBatchUsesPriorEffects, outside the required set, is refused identically with --no-preflight by validateReportBasis, so it is not a regression